// @PLN85 D-own — LIVE BUG (#457 sibling, both backends + baseline). NOT yet fixed.
//
// The match/if-EXPRESSION form `out = match { _ => { v = recurse(); v += [..]; v } }`
// drops the recursion: build(5) returns len 2 (want 5).  Matrix (both backends):
//   A match-expr `v = adopt(); v += []`  -> BROKEN (len 2)
//   B if-expr    `v = adopt(); v += []`  -> BROKEN (len 2)   [NOT match-specific]
//   C match-expr `v = adopt(); v`        -> ok (no += => no materialise)
//   D match-expr `v = [lit]; v += []`    -> ok (literal first-set)
// Trigger = arm-local + first-set is an adopting CALL + a following `+=`.
//
// ROOT (traced): an arm-local `v = recurse(..)` ADOPTS the call store but leaves
// v's dep EMPTY (the `["??"]` marker is stripped by change_var; a pre-declared
// `v: vector = []` instead keeps its own __vdb).  Then `v += [n]` -> PASS-1
// `insert_new` (gated by `vector_needs_db`, vectors.rs:2007) sees the empty dep,
// MINTS a fresh __vdb, sets v's dep to it, and emits `OpDatabase(__vdb); v =
// field(__vdb)` AFTER the adopt -> re-inits v, DROPPING the recursion (the second
// arm reuses the dep so it keeps it -> the asymmetry).  NOTE: the `+=` PASS-2
// `vector_db` (build_vector_list) is downstream of this; the real producer is the
// pass-1 `insert_new`.
//
// FIX ATTEMPT (reverted): a transient per-function marker "v adopted a vector call"
// (set at the assignment, on the var table) gating `vector_needs_db`/`insert_new`
// to skip the mint -> v appends to the adopted store IN PLACE.  This FIXED THE
// VALUE (matrix + this probe correct, both backends).  BUT it exposed the SECOND
// layer — the arm-local ADOPT/FREE: with no __vdb, v owns the adopt store and
// out's original __vdb is orphaned, and they are not freed -> a per-recursion
// LEAK that regressed 5 suite tests (p310/p171/moros/loft_suite/native_scripts).
//
// So the complete fix is TWO layers, like PR #459 did for the TAIL but for the
// match-ARM: (1) value — skip the pass-1 mint for the adopter; (2) free — deliver
// the arm into out's buffer AND free v's adopted store / out's orphaned __vdb
// (the arm-delivery free).  Both together, matrix + suite + leak both backends.
fn churn(k: integer) -> integer { z: vector<u8> = [0]; for i in 0..k { z += [1]; } return len(z); }
fn build(n: integer) -> vector<integer> {
  out: vector<integer> = [];
  if n <= 0 { return out; }
  out = match n % 2 {
    0 => { v = build(n - 1); v += [n]; v },
    _ => { v = build(n - 1); v += [n + 100]; v },
  };
  return out;
}
fn main() {
  p = build(5); churn(8);
  println("match-expr build(5): len={len(p)} (want 5) e0={p[0] ?? -1} e4={p[4] ?? -1}");
}
